The Pony Express began in 1860. It was a mail service. Horseback riders carried the mail 2,000 miles between Missouri and California. Each horse and rider went about 250 miles and then handed the mail off to the next rider. It was a hard and dangerous trip. However, only one mail delivery was ever lost. The Pony Express was most important during the first few months of the Civil War. People in California wanted to know what was happening in the war. In 1861 a telegraph wire was laid that connected the East and West Coasts. The telegraph could send messages in seconds. So, after just 19 months, the Pony Express ended.', NULL, NULL, 1, 'MAP_RC_G2-4_PAST', 'PUBLISHED') ON CONFLICT (mpg_id) DO UPDATE SET mpg_body = EXCLUDED.mpg_body, mpg_glossary = EXCLUDED.mpg_glossary, mpg_pair_group_id = EXCLUDED.mpg_pair_group_id, mpg_grade = EXCLUDED.mpg_grade, updated_at = NOW();




