Emmet paced the floor, wondering why his sister had to be so difficult. Thanks to her, he was stuck in his room. He heard something slip under his door and turned to find a piece of paper. Written on it was the statement "Guess a letter," followed by eight blank lines. Emmet crumpled the paper into a ball.

Emmet could not pass up a challenge, though, and minutes later he was smoothing out the paper. He wrote down the letter "S" and slipped the paper back under the door. He had hardly stepped away when the paper reappeared. One of the blank lines now had an "S" penciled in! Emmet wrote the letter "E" next and slid the paper back, but it returned almost immediately with no new

blanks filled in.

After several rounds of back-and-forth, Emmet was finally able to decode his sister''s secret message: "I am sorry."', NULL, NULL, 1, 'MAP_RC_G2-4_PAST', 'PUBLISHED') ON CONFLICT (mpg_id) DO UPDATE SET mpg_body = EXCLUDED.mpg_body, mpg_glossary = EXCLUDED.mpg_glossary, mpg_pair_group_id = EXCLUDED.mpg_pair_group_id, mpg_grade = EXCLUDED.mpg_grade, updated_at = NOW();




