I finally got to adopt a puppy from the shelter! Her name is Luna, and she''s brown and white with velvety soft ears. I think she''s perfect, but Gram insists that she has to go to puppy school.

I snap on Luna''s harness and open the door. She bolts down the steps, straining against the leash. By the time we get to class, I''m breathing hard, but Luna doesn''t seem tired at all. She''s darting around the other puppies, her leash dragging behind her. I call her, but she doesn''t listen. A woman without a dog catches Luna and hands me the leash. I thank her, embarrassed to realize she''s the

teacher.

"Everyone, we''re starting today with how to get your dog''s attention." she announces loudly.

I''m desperately repeating Luna''s name, but she keeps pulling toward a golden retriever. Maybe Luna does have some things to learn.

This sentence is from the passage.

