Elevators are booths or platforms that move people and goods up and down. Many people think elevators are a modern invention, but

machines that lift and lower Arst appeared thousands of years ago.

The first elevators were operated by ropes and powered by people. Some were so large it took thousands of people to run them! The first modern elevator was built in New York City in 1857. It was powered by a steam engine and was very slow. People refused to use it. At the time, bulldings were only a few stories tall, so elevators were not really needed.

Elevators became common in the 1880s when skyscrapers were built. No one wanted to dimb all those stairs. Today, elevators are in

