Sodas at School

When the soda machines were removed from our school cafeteria, I was upset. I thought it was unfair to students. Teachers and parents

said that sugary soft drinks were making students fidgety and sleepy. They predicted that students would be better off without these sugary drinks.

Although I was against removing the soda machines at first, now I believe It was a good Idea. Students have stopped drinking soda at school, and I am amazed at the results! \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_, Fewer students are getting tired after lunch. The parents and teachers were right. Soda machines in school are not good for our health or our study habits!

