"Home of the World''s Worst Weather." Many hikers climb the rocky trails to reach the summit. When skies are clear, climbers enjoy a beautiful view.

But even in summer, they are often battered by harsh conditions, including extreme wind and cold. For this reason, it is important for hikers to be cautious and well prepared. One of the most important rules is to bring warm clothing. Sunny, hot weather at the base of the mountain can change without warning to dangerous. winter-like conditions at the summit.

